  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "SeaWiFS Sea-Surface Chlorophyll Concentration Images and Data for the California Current System by University of Maine",
  "description": "GLOBEC-Pacific SeaWiFS 4 km images for the Northeast Pacific. Images are one day composites of the California Current System region. Data files in HDF format are available to registered SeaWiFS users by FTP. Contact Andrew Thomas (thomas@maine.edu) for instructions. [ Reference: PICES Scientific Report No. 18 2001, Proceedings of the PICES/CoML/IPRC Workshop on \"Impact of Climate Variability on Observation and Prediction of Ecosystem and Biodiversity Changes in the North Pacific\", http://www.pices.int/publications/scientific_reports/Report18/default.aspx. ]\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To understand the effects of climate variability and climate change on the distribution, abundance and production of marine animals (including commercially important living marine resources) in the eastern North Pacific. To embody this understanding in diagnostic and prognostic ecosystem models, capable of capturing the ecosystem response to major climatic fluctuations.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23516049",
